Declare values as array of integer with length 4. Set element at 0 in values to 10. Set element at 1 in values to 20. Set element at 2 in values to 30. Set element at 3 in values to 40. Say Element at 2 in values. Declare p as pointer to integer with value values. Say Value at (p plus 1). Say Element at 3 in p. Declare q as pointer to integer with value p plus 3. Say Value at q. Say q minus p. Say p is less than q. Set element at 1 in p to 25. Say Element at 1 in values. Add 1 to p. Say Value at p. Subtract 1 from p. Say Value at p. Say p is equal to values. Say Size of values is equal to Size of type array of integer with length 4. Declare pa as pointer to array of integer with length 4 with value Address of values. Say Element at 2 in Value at pa. Declare slots as array of pointer to integer with length 2. Set element at 0 in slots to values. Set element at 1 in slots to q. Say Value at Element at 0 in slots. Say Value at Element at 1 in slots.
